{"id":"kg-a1core-041-adjective-patterns","levelId":"a1-core","title":"Adjectives: full agreement","subtitle":"Match gender, number, and case across a noun phrase.","tags":["a1-core","adjectives","agreement"],"overview":["A regular adjective such as ἀγαθός uses first/second-declension endings to agree with its noun.","First match article and adjective; then confirm the noun."],"sections":[{"id":"forms","title":"ἀγαθός in matching phrases","kind":"table","columns":["Koine Greek","English"],"rows":[["ὁ ἀγαθὸς λόγος","the good word"],["τὸν ἀγαθὸν λόγον","the good word — object"],["ἡ ἀγαθὴ χάρις","the good grace"],["τῷ ἀγαθῷ θεῷ","to the good God"]]},{"id":"read","title":"Read agreement, not position","kind":"cards","items":[{"grc":"ὁ ἀγαθὸς ποιμὴν.","en":"the good shepherd"},{"grc":"βλέπομεν τὸ ἀγαθὸν ἔργον.","en":"We see the good work."},{"grc":"ἐν τῇ ἀγαθῇ ὁδῷ.","en":"in the good way."}]}]}
